5. RECONCILIATION WITH THE INDEPENDENT RAW-GRID PATH (analysis/verify_independent.py)
   That script re-derives everything from capital.csv alone using raw grid values (no interpolation).
   Agreement: same maximum value 4.238; same tied maxima (14th + 13th c. BCE); same own-maximum
   centuries (Copper&Gold 12th, Amber 33rd, MonumentCount 27th); same rank of the peak century.
   MonumentCount: max on RAW GRID = +3.95 at the 27th century BCE vs max of the CENTURY MEAN = +2.58 at the 27th century BCE. The raw grid concentrates a one-bin spike in a single year, so the century mean is lower; the century of the maximum is unchanged.
   Amber: max on RAW GRID = +1.54 at the 33rd century BCE vs max of the CENTURY MEAN = +1.54 at the 33rd century BCE. Identical.
   Amber full-span sign: raw grid endpoints give +0.27 (UP) while the interpolated bin means give -0.98 (DOWN) and the first3/last3 means -1.83. This is the fragility flagged in section 2; no full-span direction is claimed for Amber.
   We report the CENTURY-MEAN (interpolated) statistic as primary because it does not let one
   100-yr bin dominate a century, and the raw grid as the tie/plateau evidence.

